South Africa's trade department recommends legalising online casino gambling

South Africa's Department of Trade, Industry and Competition (DTIC) has drafted a policy recommending the legalisation of online gambling, which is currently prohibited even though online sports betting is legal. The department has consulted the provinces and the National Gambling Board and plans to open the policy for public comment this financial year, alongside a socio-economic impact assessment. Gambling GGR rose 13.4% to R84.5 billion ($4.8 billion) in 2025/26, with online betting making up 66%.

